now that we've spent a good amount of  time testing our new high-end  2025k imac it's time to start comparing  it to our other machines  like our older high-end 2017 and 2019  imacs  our 15 000 mac pro and of course my base  5 000  imac pro that i've been using daily for  a year now and that's what this video is  all about now i know a lot of you guys  are waiting to see how our lower end  i7 8 core 2020 imac compares to this  high end 10 core model  and we're actually working on that video  right now so subscribe if you want to  see those comparison videos  but before we get into comparing the  high-end imac to the imac pro  i want to show you guys our brand new  premium max tech  zip up hoodie which comes with a small  and subtle logo on the  front and the same apple product pattern  that we get on our mask  on the back of the hoodie with various  icons like the mac pro  the imac the apple watch and the new  ipad pro  so definitely check it out in our merch  shelf right below this video i'll get  into the real world performance  differences for things like logic pro 10  photo editing and video editing in just  a minute but first let's compare the  differences  in the design the ports the speakers and  the microphones  there are three main differences in  design number one is that the imac pro  gets the exclusive  space gray color which also comes on the  mouse and the larger keyboard  which comes with a numpad unlike the one  that comes with the 5k  imac number two is that the 2020 imac  gets a 500  option for the nano textured glass which  basically gives you a glare free display  without sacrificing the contrast and  color quality  like other matte display films do but we  didn't pay for this upgrade because we  don't think it's worth the 500  price and number three is the fact that  the imac pro sacrifices the user  replaceable ram door  in order to have an upgraded cooling  system with dual fans  larger heat sinks and extra exhaust  vents on the back the imac has finally  been upgraded with a 1080p webcam  just like the one on the imac pro so  here's a quick comparison of the  microphone and webcam quality  this is the new 1080p webcam on the 2020  5k imac and this is the 1080p webcam on  the 2017 imac pro as you just saw  there's not that big of a difference in  terms of the webcam  so now let's compare the speakers  [Music]  is  [Music]  hello  let me know if you heard any noticeable  differences between both machines down  in the comment section below  and now let's get into comparing the  ports both of them get four  usb a ports which are running at a  maximum speed of 5 gigabits per second  as you can see right here in the  screenshots and what's great this year  for the imac is that it supports uh s2  transfer speeds with the sd card reader  just like the one that comes on  the imac pro the 5k imac now finally has  an available  100 upgrade option to get a very fast  10 gigabit ethernet port just like the  imac pro comes with  which is great for using nas servers and  apart from that  the imac pro comes with 4 thunderbolt 3  ports  instead of just 2 on the 5k imac so with  that out of the way  let's finally get into performance but  first i want to show you guys the  differences  in the specs and i want to mention that  my imac pro  is an 8 core model but if you're buying  one new right now  the base model now comes with a 10 core  so keep that in mind  and you'll also notice that because the  5k imac has a ram door  we bought 64 gigs of ram for only 240  on amazon and upgraded it ourselves  giving it an  advantage over the imac pro which  actually has a larger ssd  at the base price but either way the 5k  imac  is significantly cheaper and with that  let's get right into our performance  comparison  starting with a fan noise test which we  ran by using a terminal script  that maxes out the cpu and the fan noise  you're about to hear  is after exactly five minutes of running  the script on each mac  so let me know what you think about the  fan noise differences down in the  comments below  and now let's finally get into the  benchmarks starting with geekbench 5  cpu test in terms of single core  performance  the imac kills the imac pro so if you're  doing tasks that only use  one core there's going to be a huge  advantage for the regular imac  and in terms of multi-core score we see  basically the same results  with over 20 percent more raw multi-core  performance  using the 10 core cpu on the new imac  now running the cinebench r20 cpu stress  test  the 5k imac somehow scored 50 higher  than the imac pro which is super  impressive now let's get into graphics  performance  starting with geekbench 5's metal test  and here  the imax 5700 xt outperformed the imac  pros vega 56  by just a little bit we then tested  unigine's heaven gaming benchmark on the  extreme preset  and the imac scored around 22 more fps  than the imac pro which is definitely  more along the lines of what we were  expecting  and we actually played some games on  windows 10 using bootcamp and it  performed  very well so definitely check out our  gaming review after this video  now since unigine heaven uses opengl we  also ran some metal benchmarks  using gfx bench 5.0 in the aztec ruins  test  the 5k imac scored around 25 more fps  than the imac pro and in the manhattan  test there was a smaller  difference since we were already close  to reaching 400 fps in that test  now one thing i do want to mention  before we move on is that the 5700 xt in  the imac  comes with 16 gigs of vram compared to 8  gigs with  the vega 56 on the imac pro  but the bandwidth on the imac pro is  actually a little bit higher  with 400 gigabytes per second of  bandwidth now before we finally get into  our video editing tests with final cut  pro 10  let's test everything from photo editing  logic pro 10 music production  and xcode programming we ran the puget  bench photoshop benchmark  and the 5k imac actually scored around  35 percent higher  than the imac pro which is pretty  surprising and we think the difference  is due to the extra cores  and the extra ram we then exported 500  raw  42 megapixel photos in lightroom classic  and we saw the complete opposite result  the imac pro  actually finished 5 minutes faster than  the 5k imac  even though it was 35 slower in puget  bench for photoshop  and then we created 50 raw one-to-one  previews  and the imac pro was 16 seconds faster  in this test as well  so it's definitely a better choice but  this result just doesn't make sense  considering the raw performance  difference we did a little bit of  digging and we realized that the imac  pro is  actually using 4 channel memory compared  to only dual channel on  the imac which is allowing it to perform  better  even though it has two times less  physical ram now moving on to the max  tech  xcode benchmark created for us by max  aramenko  which you can find a link to in the  description the 5k imac was a little  over  20 faster than the imac pro thanks to  the extra cpu performance  now getting into music production we ran  the new logic pro 10 benchmark 2  which tests how many tracks the system  can handle without getting an  overload error message and surprisingly  the imac pro was able to play 31 more  tracks  than the 5k imac before overloading the  reason for that is because the imac pro  uses  server grade xeon chips that are more  reliable  and run at more stable clock speeds but  if you're not trying to max out the  system with tons of tracks  the 5k imac should perform just as well  for day-to-day music production  and now finally getting into final cut  pro 10 the imac was surprisingly over 50  faster in the bruce x 5k benchmark  which we think is due to the differences  in raw performance  and the new navi based graphics  architecture in the 5700 xt  then moving on to our 1 minute 4k hevc  stabilization test  the 5k imac destroyed the imac pro  by finishing four times faster which  didn't make any sense  but then we dug deeper and realized that  the 5k imac is using  quick sync to encode which the imac pro  doesn't have  because it lacks an integrated graphics  chip now onto our 5 minute 4k  h.264 export test which is basically the  most common format that youtubers use  the 5k imac was just 3 seconds faster  than the imac pro  so it's not that big of a difference so  because of that  this year we're adding a brand new h.264  test  exporting one of our very own videos  which is 12 minutes long  and packs a bunch of effects and graphs  that we use  all the time in our videos so it's just  about the most  real world test you can get here the 5k  imac shows its true colors  finishing the export almost a minute and  a half quicker  than the imac pro so for regular 4k  h.264 editing  the imac is definitely the better choice  and for a lower price  now what about hevc editing which is  quickly becoming the new  standard well in our five minute export  test  the 5k imac was just 3 seconds faster  since both machines are limited by the  encoding speed of the t2 chip  which handles hevc footage and i do want  to mention that the navi graphics card  in the imac  actually has new hevc encoders that run  at 90 frames per second compared to the  t2 chips  60 fps but final cut hasn't yet been  updated to support these new navi  encoders  but when it eventually does in the  future the 5k imac should get even  faster for hevc editing now a lot of you  guys have been asking us to edit canon's  422  eos r5 footage and it actually improved  with the new final cut pro 10.4.9 update  so if you want more info on that max  actually made a video on his other  channel focusing on that new codec  so i'll link to that video in the end  screen after this one's over  but i did run a transcoding test on a 30  minute canon r5 clip  and the 5k imac finished the transcode  quite a bit faster  than the imac pro so there's that now  moving on to canon c200 raw footage  the new final cut pro update broke it so  we're currently waiting on canon to  release the new raw plug-in so we ran  our  minute export test using the previous  version of final cut pro  and the 5k imac finished over three  minutes faster  than the imac pro and in terms of the  playback fps in the timeline  both of them played the footage at a  perfect 60 60fps  which is very impressive now moving on  to redraw editing  we ran the new version of final cut pro  with the new raw plug-in  and the 5k imac easily killed the imac  pro  finishing our 5-minute 4.5 k export in  exactly 5 minutes  and then moving on to the 8k redraw test  the 5k imac finished a very impressive  4 minutes faster than the imac pro and  the new final cut pro update helps a  huge amount  since it used to take over 17 minutes  using the previous 10.4.8 version  of final cut and in terms of playing  back this ak footage  the 5k imac can run it at around 19 fps  out of 24  while the imac pro runs it at around 15  fps  so there you guys go from all of these  tests that we ran  we can conclude that the 5k imac is  better for  almost everything including video  editing  programming with xcode graphic design  with photoshop  and gaming as well but the imac pro  actually performed better  for lightroom classic photo editing  thanks to the quad channel ram  and it handled more tracks in logic pro  10  thanks to the more stable server grade  xeon chip and thankfully  the port situation has been improved  with the 5k imac  now that it finally has a faster sd card  slot and an option for a 10 gig ethernet  port  but the imac pro still has the advantage  of two extra thunderbolt 3 ports  so with all that said if we're looking  at the entire system in general  the 5k imac is obviously the better  choice  because it's more powerful overall it's  less expensive  it gets newer technology like the navi  graphics architecture  and it has the ram door so you can save  a lot of money by upgrading the ram  yourself  especially for those who want to get 128  gigs of ram  for just 500 on amazon instead of paying  two thousand dollars for it  on the imac pro so there you guys have  it hopefully this comparison video  helped you make a decision and if it did  go ahead and click the circle above to  subscribe  because we've got a heck of a lot more  imac videos to come very soon  and definitely check out our apple  product merch down below including our  brand new  apple product zip up hoodie so thank you  guys for watching and we'll see you in  the next one  you

